{title: 144 - O Sing a Song of Bethlehem}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Am]O sing [C/G]a song of [D/F#]Bethlehem,
[C/G]Of shepherds [Bm/D]watching [C]there,
[C/G]And [G]of the news [C/G]that [Em/B]came to them
[D/F#]From angels [G]in the [D7/C]air:
[D7/F#]The light [G]that shone [Em]on Bethlehem
[G]Fills all [Bm]the world [D7/C]today;
[Em/B]Of [D]Jesus'birth [G/D]and [D7/C]peace on [Em/B]earth
[Em/G]The angels sing [G]alway.

Verse 2:
[Am]O sing [C/G]a song of [D/F#]Nazareth,
[C/G]Of sunny [Bm/D]days [C]of joy,
[C/G]O [G]sing of fragrant [Em/B]flowers breath,
[D/F#]And of [G]the sinless [D7/C]Boy:
[D7/F#]For now the [G]flowers [Em]of Nazareth
[G]In every [Bm/D]heart [D7/C]may grow;
[Em/B]Now [D]spreads the [G]fame of [D7/C]His dear [Em/B]name
[Em/G]On all the winds [G]that blow.

Verse 3:
[Am]O sing [C/G]a song of [D/F#]Calvary,
[C/G]Its glory [Bm/D]and [C]dismay;
[C/G]Of [G]Him who hung [C/G]upon [Em/G]the tree,
[D/F#]And took [G]our sins away:
[D7/F#]For He [G]who died [Em]on Calvary
[G]Is risen [Bm/D]from [D7/C]the grave;
[Em/B]And Christ, [D]our Lord, [G]by heaven [D7/C]adored,
[Em/G]Is mighty now [G]to save.
